<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I9aa4db3bdfe55f1d8e870c03010e76512570a48d" commit="211f704692a266ebf6e18de17b1bd9fd605668e0" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: patch kernel to support SW Shortcut Forwarding Engine (SFE)  1. To support SFE 1.1 Added a hook in netif_receive_skb() to pass packet to SFE     for acceleration. 1.2 Added a field fast_forwarded in sk_buff to skip some heavy     processing in kernel.  2. To support multiple listeners of connection event 2.1 Multiple modules need to listen on connection events.     &quot;net-&gt;ct.nf_conntrack_event_cb&quot; can support only one listener,     so we replaced it with a notification chain &quot;net-&gt;ct.nf_conntrack_chain&quot;     to support multiple listeners.  3. To update stats on bridge interface 3.1 Added a new function br_dev_update_stats in Linux bridge.     Fast-classifier has an option to skip bridge processing for     routed packets. So Fast-classifier need this function to update     stats on bridge interface.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56410 TEST=DK04. In addition, ran throughput tests on a wired client with multiple streams.  Change-Id: I9aa4db3bdfe55f1d8e870c03010e76512570a48d Signed-off-by: Xiaoping Fan &lt;xfan@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361050 Commit-Ready: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Hayes &lt;kevinhayes@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="361050" owner_email="xfan@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/50/361050/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie982abbc5505cd