ber="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/76/378376/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia0255c6a9791cbafd34a56c7f33ef003f89c499c" commit="4ac1afaf060ef80e74a62216f170439d8a684909" commit_message="cleanup: remote dead server/tests code  I see no meaningful changes here since 2011, other than fixes as parts of refactor to the rest of the codebase.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ia0255c6a9791cbafd34a56c7f33ef003f89c499c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/378377 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="378377" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/77/378377/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8b1ae8f75cd326334e50c3308b0106d1e3a4d798" commit="78c6f81b0723800e94dbf9e8645056e24ed79dd0" commit_message="login: Add PrioritizeArcInstance dbus method  Once CL:380327 is landed, ARC processes will run in a restricted cgroups by default so that booting ARC won't slow down Chrome's user session restoration. However, we also need a way to remove the restriction so that ARC apps can run full speed once the user actually starts using them.  This CL provides a new D-Bus method called PrioritizeArcInstance to allow Chrome to remove the cgroups restriction as needed.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56555 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=cyan --packages chromeos-login TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=rambi --packages chromeos-login TEST=Manually checked that Chrome can actually call the method. CQ-DEPEND=CL:383074  Change-Id: I8b1ae8f75cd326334e50c3308b0106d1e3a